I haven't followed it in a couple of years, but there was a variant of
Angband (Cthangband, IIRC) that used many of the Lovecraftian
characters as unique monsters in place of the Tolkein characters.  I
don't recall any copyright issues arising with that game.  In fact, I
don't quite see how using the name/characteristics of a character from
a book infringes copyrights.  Copyright deals with making copies or
clearly derivative works without permission.  I don't think inserting
a few Lovecraftian characters into an existing game would make it a
derivative work, but that's a legal gray area best left to the
lawyers...

